workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:11:- **Cadence derivation (printed, not just scheduled):** while OWED + IN-PROGRESS items outnumber the RECREATED pool, waves fire every **3 h** — at wave 5 that is up to 40 first attempts/day against a 22-item backlog (≈0.6 days nominal to clear, before digestion adds more). As the catalogue approaches mostly-RECREATED, cadence relaxes toward maintenance — the relaxation is a printed judgment with its reason, filed as an amendment + reported, never a silent schedule drift.
workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:32:- **Plan's standing product:** the Execute checklist (§3 steps as an itemized list) AND the Verify checklist (each deliverable property with its checking instrument — swap-test altered values, purity grep patterns, comparison check, jev-prewave call point, five-lens wave composition) AND the failure-point evaluation (per item, priced from this job's record: convergent freeze · intensity collapse · phrase overlap · fitting limits · render-proof limitation), all in RUN.md at this gate.
workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:47:2. **Construction purity (own, mechanical):** grep the recreation for the original's media (segment filename, source filename, frame-sequence patterns, <video>/<img> pointing at specimen media) — any hit is a refusal-class defect (§6.1). Asset inventory: every asset the recreation loads is listed and is either code or generated/created by this build.
workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:73:**Re-attempt floor rule:** a re-attempt whose average does NOT beat the technique's prior attempt average is not filed as silent progress — its scores.md entry carries a WHY section naming the plateau (what was changed, what did not move, which lens is stuck and the hypothesized cause). Grinding the same score without a named plateau is the ceremony pattern in miniature and is a deviation (PLATEAU-UNNAMED) in the attempt's RUN. Score deltas are reported in the library's growth accounting (style-library GROWTH.md) per attempt, not only at consolidation.
workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:88:Read the run's traces + Codex returns → candidate lessons (which constructions scored well on which lenses; recurring Codex findings across techniques) → label demonstrated/candidate/planned → promote into this file (dated, technique cited) + verdict-history.md → next cycle inherits. A lens finding that recurs across two techniques is a pattern: it becomes a §6 guard candidate with the two citations.
workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md:89:- **Condense Codex call point:** `guards/codex-condense.md` fires at Condense close — it attacks the cycle's drafted amendments for faithfulness (does the amended text encode the lesson) and four-layer coverage (steps · mechanical guards · Jev definitions · Codex prompts; each untouched layer carries a NO-DEFECT proof or a named not-yet-amended reason). A REVISE returns the named amendment for re-encoding before the cycle record closes. Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE. (Built 2026-11-14.)
