**REVISE — Firing 2. The re-encoding fixes the sequencing distinction, Jev’s HOLD rule, and T219’s score citations. §9 still omits a guard miss and overstates what the receipts and close records establish.**

Consumer and working record — Recreation Cycle 040 Condense, for filing in §9b. I reviewed the on-disk Cycle 040 `RUN.md`, governing instructions and guards, prior Condense dispositions, payloads, filed returns, and close records.

1. **Keep the HQ deferral and narrow the lesson in §9.1.** Cycle 037 `RUN.md` §9b.1 supports the deferral on `INSTRUCTION.md` §5 leg 3b and the mechanical guard layer. T227’s completion return confirms that Observe/Plan §2.3 already required full-state equality. The draft still infers that “the defect set is not a fixed checklist a builder can exhaust by care alone.” T227 shows an existing requirement went unchecked. T219’s clearance shows its corrected CP1 receipt and index reconciliations satisfied prewave for that item. State the observed result across the wave: builder reconciliation again let deficient receipts reach prewave. The cause and the proposed validator’s effectiveness remain unestablished.

2. **Add T233’s measured-fit miss to the mechanical disposition.** §9.3(2) now names T218 under command 6, with coverage supported by Cycle 039 §9.3(2), and scopes command 4 to T219. But T233’s `codex/jev-prewave-2.md`, findings 3–4, identifies **both** missing CONFIG census entries and a separate fit miss. The tool-label row measured horizontal clearance while omitting the vertical edge. The return derives a baseline of −102 px from `188 − (6 × 36)/2 − 170 − 12`. Record three misses across two commands, add the T233 fit miss to the command-6 deferral, and qualify T233’s filed zero-hit summaries for both legs. Cycle 037’s acceptance test names other cases, so identify the new fit and census cases as additional evidence for HQ.

3. **Separate gate dispositions from completed verification, and carry the Plan-exit feeder gap.** The T233 payload and return order supports §7 D4, and `item-T233-observe-plan.md` §2b supports the separate A9.2 pre-build finding. That same §2b records that the Plan-exit payload excerpt omitted command 8. `item-T233-jev-plan-exit-return.md` marks the command **UNVERIFIED** in its Limits. Carry that omission under the FED completeness deferral, alongside the separately verified `BODY-WRITE` omission in all four completion payloads and returns. Also narrow §9.3(4)’s claim that the P11 coverage cure is in the built artifact. The Plan carries the cure, but T233’s final prewave return, findings 1–2, shows that the harness prints the P11 post-swap diff without enforcing equality and runs census calls at literal times. Record those verification receipts as still owed. The Jev verdicts can stand with that qualification.

4. **Keep the direct score citations and make the scoring-prompt disposition explicit.** T219’s five filed lens returns give `92 + 100 + 100 + 87 + 84 = 463`, so the average is **92.6** and the minimum **84**. §9.2 now binds the overlap, CP9 label, metadata, and contrast notes to the right returns. The stale-text deferral also names the two additional locations from firing 1. For `guards/codex-scoring-wave.md` itself, state the scoped no-change finding against its five-lens form and timing-mapping requirement. The five filed returns and `payload-T219-lens-timing.txt` supply that evidence.

5. **File or qualify the close claims.** The on-disk Cycle 040 `RUN.md` ends at §7 and has no §9b, although §9.5 says every review return was dispositioned and §7 marks Condense accounted. The firing 1 return exists as a separate file. The close records also still show the pre-close state: `HQ.json` has `rec-2026-11-18-wave37` as `planned`, heartbeat beat 126 is the skeleton, and `verdict-history.md` and `QUEUE.md` end at Wave 36. Record §9b and the delivery writes as pending until filed and read back. §9.4’s cost accounting stands: **6 prewave + 4 Phase A + 5 lenses = 15** returns, or **3 per item** and **15 per scored verdict**. Elapsed per-item cost is unassessed. On the draft’s counts, both `1 + 12 = 13` and `9 + 12 = 21` fall below 72, and the draft records retention of the three-hour schedule without claiming a measured re-price. Label those as post-wave counts pending the queue update.

**Limits** — This was a record and receipt review. I did not replay the recreations, rerun the harnesses, or re-score the wave.

